// Greedy bounds: a disjunction of two bounds on the same clock (x >= 999 || x >= 1000) requests sleep only up to
// the later bound, but the transition already fires at the earlier one. sleepT counts every state active in the
// tick, including one that is just being left, as long as its clock is still below the bound (x < bound).
scchart St73Greedy {
  output int n = 0
  clock x
  initial state S
  if x >= 999 || x >= 1000 do x = 0; n++ go to S
}
